# Unity's YAML serializer for MonoBehaviour/ScriptableObject-backed assets
# (ProjectSettings/*.asset, scenes, prefabs, materials, etc.) writes a single
# trailing space on fields whose string value is empty (e.g. m_Name,
# m_EditorClassIdentifier) every time the asset is resaved by the Editor —
# reproduced deterministically across repeated imports of this project. That
# is Unity's own canonical serialized form, not an error to flag or strip;
# stripping it would just have Unity re-add it on the next Editor launch.
*.unity -whitespace
*.prefab -whitespace
*.asset -whitespace
*.mat -whitespace
*.controller -whitespace
*.anim -whitespace
*.overrideController -whitespace
*.physicMaterial -whitespace
*.physicsMaterial2D -whitespace
*.renderTexture -whitespace
*.spriteatlas -whitespace
*.terrainlayer -whitespace
*.guiskin -whitespace
*.preset -whitespace
*.playable -whitespace
*.mask -whitespace
*.brush -whitespace
*.flare -whitespace
*.fontsettings -whitespace

